\details{
The user inputs for this module are separated from the outputs to allow for
more flexible UI design.

The module is the interactive counterpart of \code{\link[dittoSeq:dittoHeatmap]{dittoSeq::dittoHeatmap()}}: the
expression of chosen genes across the cells (or samples) of a
\code{SingleCellExperiment}, \code{SummarizedExperiment} or \code{Seurat} object, with cell
metadata as annotation tracks. The expression matrix is pulled with
\code{dittoHeatmap(data.out = TRUE)} and drawn by
\code{\link[VizModules:ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI]{VizModules::ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI()}}, so its scaling, clustering,
splitting, colour, label and annotation controls all apply; those inputs
are documented there. Every metadata column is available as a column
annotation; the cell identifier is the \code{cell} column (the column key).

\strong{This module is not plotly.} It renders through InteractiveComplexHeatmap
(hover, click and brush a region for a sub-heatmap), so the shared plotly
tabs (Axes, Legend, Lines, Plotly) do not apply, and it needs ComplexHeatmap,
InteractiveComplexHeatmap and circlize. Genes that do not vary across the
cells are dropped, since they cannot be scaled or clustered.
}
