\section{Plot parameters and defaults}{

The following parameters can be accessed via UI inputs and/or the \code{defaults} argument:
\itemize{
\item \code{dh.genes} - Genes to show (UI: "Genes", default: the 20 most variable genes;
dittoSeq \code{genes})
\item \code{dh.assay} - Assay (UI: "Assay", default: dittoSeq's default, \code{logcounts}
when present; dittoSeq \code{assay})
\item \code{dh.order.by} - Metadata column the cells are ordered by, or \code{""} for the
object's order (UI: "Order Cells By", default: the first discrete metadata
column; dittoSeq \code{order.by})
\item \code{annot.by} - Metadata columns shown as column annotations when the module
opens (default: the first discrete metadata column; dittoSeq \code{annot.by}).
Not an input: further tracks are added on the Annotations tab.
\item Wrapped heatmap defaults set here: \code{scale = "Rows"}, \code{cluster_columns = FALSE}, \code{show_column_dend = FALSE}, \code{show_column_names} (only for 50 or
fewer cells), \code{name = "Expression"}
\item All other \code{\link[VizModules:ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI]{VizModules::ComplexHeatmap_HeatmapInputsUI()}} parameters, except
\code{matrix.cols} and \code{rowname.col}, which the module sets
